LIMITATIONS -- read before citing any number above:
  * RECONSTRUCTION, not a live run. The decision function is applied
    to rows rebuilt from committed post-clobber artifacts by putting
    back only the four fields the clobber wrote.
  * RESIDUAL BOUND. The disagree branch is reachable here through
    species_name and taxonomy_id ONLY. species/organism are
    re-stamped from the ref and agree by construction;
    species_id/pathbank_species_id are set equal to the ref id or
    dropped, so their guard cannot fire. A contradiction living only
    in those fields would be invisible to this probe.
  * REV-099 Finding 2: the previous version built a fresh dict from
    the ref, so NO field could disagree and its 'PRESERVED 4' was an
    upper bound. This version is a measurement only to the extent the
    per-row 'live' column above says the check actually ran.
  * Where a ref carries no species id the pre-clobber id is
    unrecoverable; those rows have their id fields dropped rather
    than guessed, which is one of two possible reconstructions.
  * Contradictions a live run would create after the mapping stage
    cannot appear here; only mapping-stage artifacts are read.
